dts: rename the Mali GPU interrupts to the names kbase requests.

The vendor Mali kbase driver requests its IRQs by the names "JOB",
"MMU" and "GPU"; the tree's gpu node names them lowercase, so every
boot logs three "IRQ ... not found" errors before kbase falls back to
the lowercase names. Rename to the uppercase set kbase tries first.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi	2026-07-26 11:34:15
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi	2026-07-26 11:34:15
@@ -2668,7 +2668,7 @@
 		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 349 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 			<GIC_SPI 348 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 			<GIC_SPI 347 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
-		interrupt-names = "gpu", "mmu", "job";
+		interrupt-names = "GPU", "MMU", "JOB";
 
 		upthreshold = <40>;
 		downdifferential = <10>;
